LitLoop is maintained independently by dysprosium231 and is not affiliated
with or endorsed by the original authors. The full commit history of the
original project is preserved in this repository; changes made for LitLoop
are the commits after upstream commit fb796df and include:

- Institutional downloads: fixes for browser-based publisher logins (WebVPN,
  CARSI/Shibboleth, school-agnostic IdP detection, login heartbeat so races
  wait for a user who is logging in, cancellation of in-flight downloads).
- Browser: option to drive a copy of the locally installed Chrome; stable
  browser process name; per-host proxy exception for publishers that
  authorise by cookie; challenge-page and PDF-capture fixes for Science,
  Springer Nature, RSC, ACS, Wiley and AIP.
- Sci-Hub: ALTCHA proof-of-work solved over HTTP so it works without a
  browser; optional no-browser mode; mirror-probe fix.
- Zotero: zotero_push files papers through zotero-mcp (CrossRef metadata,
  duplicate reuse, PDF attachment to WebDAV) and finds it automatically.
- Installation: scripts/deploy.py installs or updates the plugin end to end
  and registers it with Claude Code, Claude Desktop and Codex.
- Config output masks every API key; Springer OA-only keys are recognised.

The compiled extensions of the original project (src/scansci_pdf/_core/*.pyd,
*.so) are distributed by the original authors via PyPI only and are NOT part
of this repository; LitLoop uses the pure-Python fallbacks.

